### Field Definitions

#### abilities table
| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| (key) | number | Yes | Spell ID |
| level | number | Yes | Minimum level to learn |
| cost | number | Yes | Cost in copper (100 = 1 silver, 10000 = 1 gold) |

#### talents table
| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| (key) | number | Yes | Spell ID |
| tree | number | Yes | Tree index (1, 2, or 3) |
| tier | number | Yes | Tier/row (1, 2, or 3) |
| prerequisite | number | No | Spell ID that must be maxed first |
| column | number | No | Force specific column (1, 2, or 3). Auto-assigned if omitted |

## Talent Rank Detection

### Automatic Grouping
System groups spell IDs into talent families by:
1. Query spell name from `spell_dbc` or lookup table
2. Group by (spell_name, source_class)

```lua
-- {{{ groupTalentRanks
-- Groups talent spell IDs into families by name + source class
function CustomClasses.groupTalentRanks(talents)
    local families = {}

    for spellId, config in pairs(talents) do
        local spellName = GetSpellName(spellId)
        local sourceClass = GetSpellSourceClass(spellId)
        local key = spellName .. "_" .. sourceClass

        if not families[key] then
            families[key] = {
                name = spellName,
                sourceClass = sourceClass,
                tree = config.tree,
                tier = config.tier,
                prerequisite = config.prerequisite,
                ranks = {},
            }
        end

        table.insert(families[key].ranks, spellId)
    end

    -- Sort ranks by spell ID (usually correlates with rank order)
    for _, family in pairs(families) do
        table.sort(family.ranks)
    end

    return families
end -- }}}
```

### Skipped Ranks
If user defines only some ranks, system renumbers for display:

```lua
-- User defines:
[16462] = { tree = 1, tier = 1 },  -- Warrior Deflection R1 (+1%)
[16464] = { tree = 1, tier = 1 },  -- Warrior Deflection R3 (+3%)
[16466] = { tree = 1, tier = 1 },  -- Warrior Deflection R5 (+5%)

-- System displays:
-- "Deflection" with 3 ranks
-- Rank 1: +1% parry (spell 16462)
-- Rank 2: +3% parry (spell 16464)  -- Was R3, now displayed as R2
-- Rank 3: +5% parry (spell 16466)  -- Was R5, now displayed as R3

-- Player spends 3 talent points, gets full +5% effect
-- Effectively "compressed" the 5-rank talent into 3 ranks
```

